# API Contract — Generate Optimal Route

## Operation

POST /api/routes/optimize

## Purpose

Generate an optimized delivery route from selected delivery
nodes and an available driver.

## Actor

Fleet Dispatcher

## Request

{
  "deliveryNodeIds": [
    "DN001",
    "DN002",
    "DN003"
  ],
  "driverId": "DRV001"
}

## Validation Rules

1. At least one delivery node must be supplied.
2. All delivery nodes must exist.
3. Delivery nodes must have valid geographic coordinates.
4. Delivery nodes must have a Pending status.
5. The driver must exist.
6. The driver must be Available.
7. Only an authenticated Fleet Dispatcher may perform this operation.

## Business Rules

1. Only available drivers may receive a new route.
2. A delivery node cannot belong to two active routes.
3. Routes exceeding standard shift hours require manual review.
4. The dispatcher must review and confirm the generated route
   before it becomes Active.

## Successful Response

HTTP 200 OK

{
  "routeId": "RT001",
  "driverId": "DRV001",
  "status": "Draft",
  "waypoints": [
    {
      "deliveryNodeId": "DN002",
      "sequence": 1,
      "eta": "10:35"
    },
    {
      "deliveryNodeId": "DN001",
      "sequence": 2,
      "eta": "10:52"
    },
    {
      "deliveryNodeId": "DN003",
      "sequence": 3,
      "eta": "11:15"
    }
  ]
}

## Error Outcomes

400 INVALID_REQUEST
401 UNAUTHORIZED
403 FORBIDDEN
404 DRIVER_NOT_FOUND
409 DRIVER_UNAVAILABLE
409 NODE_ALREADY_ASSIGNED
422 INVALID_NODE_STATUS
422 ROUTE_EXCEEDS_SHIFT
503 OPTIMIZATION_UNAVAILABLE

## Processing Flow

Dispatcher
    ↓
Validate Request
    ↓
Validate Driver and Delivery Nodes
    ↓
Optimization Engine
    ↓
Calculate Route Sequence and ETAs
    ↓
Return Draft Route
    ↓
Dispatcher Reviews and Confirms
    ↓
Assign Route to Driver
    ↓
Route becomes Active
